<title>USA: Fidelity sets flat fee for online trades. [CORRECTED 20:20 GMT]</title>
<headline>Fidelity sets flat fee for online trades. [CORRECTED 20:20 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Investments said on Monday that it will offer a flat commission rate as low as $28.95 for all customers who place trades for stocks or mutual funds online.</p>
<p>The flat fee applies to stock trades made through the website www.fidelity.com or through the Fidelity Online Xpress+ trading software or to trades of mutual funds made through the mutual fund supermarket FundsNetwork.</p>
<p>The new price is effective immediately.</p>
<p>(Corrects from October 1).</p>
<p>((-- Boston bureau, (617) 367-4106))</p>
